--
-- delegation_task — the BMP week 9 accountability layer. ONE-TIME tasks with a
-- date, a person, and a score that gets read aloud in the executive meeting.
--
-- THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO RECURRENCE COLUMN (decision G5). Recurring work
-- belongs on a checklist. A repeating task here either scores once, making the
-- repetition pointless, or scores every occurrence and drowns genuine one-time
-- commitments under routine ticks.
--
-- FOUR CHECK CONSTRAINTS, and they are in the database rather than only in a
-- server action for the reason F11 gives: a rule that lives only in TypeScript
-- is a rule a psql session does not have.
--
--   done_needs_completed_at    Done with no date has nothing for days_late to
--                              measure, so the task finishes at no cost.
--   blocked_needs_note         "Blocked" with no note reads as a reason and
--                              carries no information.
--   completed_at_only_when_done  v_delegation_status reads completed_at FIRST.
--                              A date left behind on a task moved back to In
--                              Progress would freeze its lateness at the old
--                              value — a wrong score with no error.
--   expected_after_given       A task cannot be due before it was given.
--
-- date_given defaults to today_ist(), not now()::date. C10: every date boundary
-- in this system is Asia/Kolkata, and a task delegated at 9am IST on the 3rd is
-- 03:30 UTC — same day — while one at 2am IST is the previous day in UTC.
-- ===========================================================================

